msgid "Running a Script in SITL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:10
#: fec931203a4049288582b94f7ac85675
msgid "In Linux:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:12
#: 112a01aaa7b2490da5a1e7c337ac96a5
msgid "Assuming you have setup the build and SITL environment, run SITL. See :ref:`using-sitl-for-ardupilot-testing`. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:19
#: ff27d35abb6842aaa2473c8e734ac691
msgid "Mavproxy ground control station will automatically be started. You can also start QGC (using the QGroundControl.AppImage) and/or Mission Planner (using WISE to run under Linux). Any or all three can be used simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:21
#: 7b66d5bd1eaf438cb555380a30f52341
msgid "From your GCS, enable scripting by setting the :ref:`SCR_ENABLE<SCR_ENABLE>` parameter to \"1\". Restart the simulation by halting it with CTRL+C and restarting sim_vehicle, or in MAVProxy, type ``reboot``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:22
#: 4709c0da332042b8818af329e028f9ba
msgid "A \"scripts\" sub-directory will be created in the directory you started the simulation, if it did not already exist. You should expect to see a line similar to the following: ``Lua: State memory usage: 4824 + 9263``. This shows that scripting is now enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:23
#: 295b1945c9d14713862bc791f550e07e
msgid "Now, create your first script in the ``scripts`` folder. If it's your first time, try the hello world script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:29
#: 91207e411ac242fbb96caa6f3a28df22
msgid "Again, restart the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:30
#: dd9618bb7d634137a741ecdac635c702
msgid "You should now observe the following in console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:35
#: afb4edbc9a5e4eccbe748c9bb2e35a17
msgid "Now, you can try changing the script to say something else and saving the Lua script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:36
#: 8861e27c24924afb85ff97cd67318b2b
msgid "In MAVProxy, once you you save changes to your Lua script, you can just restart the scripting engine with ``scripting restart``. This allows to you keep SITL running and quickly change your script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:37
#: 286bf632216d4eff82186bb58a77d937
msgid "If you get a \"Scripting: out of memory\" GCS message then you will need to increase :ref:`SCR_HEAP_SIZE<SCR_HEAP_SIZE>` parameter and try to restart the simulation. The hello world script has enough memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:39
#: 5f553ef604724afaa876c2625dc8403e
msgid "In Mission Planner (Windows):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:41
#: 08c1217e59fa4c6aa1ad80023637a26c
msgid "Start the simulation in Mission Planner as normal (see :ref:`mission-planner-simulation`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:42
#: 3831153c48ad4a5b9422a0f781f5e9ae
msgid "In the CONFIG->Full Parameter List, set the :ref:`SCR_ENABLE<SCR_ENABLE>` parameter to \"1\". Restart the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:43
#: b0b6f668fc7f4a4d95c16b2bbb4aa17c
msgid "The 'scripts' subdirectory will be located in your Documents->Mission Planner->sitl directory.Place the script you downloaded into this directory. Again, restart the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:44
#: de642c92e7e24734a61ff1f5ed1e09bc
msgid "If you get a \"Scripting: out of memory\" GCS message then you will need to increase the :ref:`SCR_HEAP_SIZE<SCR_HEAP_SIZE>` parameter and try to restart the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:47
#: 07ee7d7f267a498cb8467b9fa3d881c8
msgid "Running a script on your Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:49
#: d6fe8960ca10404092244ef5044bdde4
msgid "Connect your GCS and navigate to its parameters screen (CONFIG->Full Parameter List in Mission Planner, Vehicle Setup->Parameters in QGC) . Enable :ref:`SCR_ENABLE<SCR_ENABLE>` =1. Disconnect and reconnect the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:50
#: 24878ecea2ac42c49d6c1fdc39caa8d7
msgid "On your SD card, place the script in the APM/scripts directory. This directory will be created on the SD card when you have enabled the :ref:`SCR_ENABLE<SCR_ENABLE>` via your GCS. If it does not exist, create it and load the script. You can use Mission Planner's CONFIG->MAVFTP tab or take out the SD card and use a PC to write the script onto the card."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:51
#: 0f97cb2f7cd442d4a1af10f5206cd12d
msgid "Restart the autopilot with the SD card in and the script(s) on it will load and execute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:52
#: c181a11be8fa4c95aa060e5a4d21fff5
msgid "If you get a \"Scripting: out of memory\" GCS message then you will need to increase :ref:`SCR_HEAP_SIZE<SCR_HEAP_SIZE>` parameter and try to restart the simulation. How much memory is needed is dependent on the script and the configuration of peripherals and features in use on the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:55
#: 7fe05ebfbacf4908a3c14aa0600d5dad
msgid "Once Script is running"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:57
#: eb45157461104b309f29c63322bebee3
msgid "Many scripts will require parameters created by the script to be setup or RC switches configured. This should be explained in the script's README.md file co-located with the script in the ArduPilot repo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-scripting-step-by-step.rst:59
#: dfc8403dfdef4f4a83be9ecf9940a690
msgid "You can stop or restart scripting operations from the RC transmitter (see :ref:`Auxiliary switches <common-auxiliary-functions>`) or via MAVLink command (GCS)."
msgstr ""
